abstract: >
  AetherIdentity is a candidate eighth functional dimension of the Aether
  family. It investigates whether identity proof, continuity, reputation,
  Sybil resistance, and delegation in multi-agent software ecosystems
  constitute a genuine gap not already covered by the seven existing
  dimensions. v2.0.0 is an experimental reference implementation of the
  v1.0.0 paper. It implements L1–L5 and a minimal independent simulator.
  It does not implement network transport, consensus, or AetherMesh
  integration. No real-world deployment has been evaluated.
